 "result_text": "Predicates now survive a JSON round trip. I ran a small `Chain` with an `is_in` predicate in `edge_match` through `Chain.from_json(c.to_json())`, and the result serialized back to identical JSON. I didn't run the test suite, and I didn't try your exact chain with the Caribbean bank list.\n\nThe cause was in `maybe_filter_dict_from_json` in `graphistry/compute/ast.py`. It called `ASTPredicate.from_json` on the abstract base class, so it never looked up the concrete predicate type (`IsIn`, `GT` and so on). I switched it to the type-dispatching `from_json` in `graphistry/compute/predicates/from_json.py`. This covers `filter_dict`, `edge_match`, `source_node_match` and `destination_node_match`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
